.TH LOCALPASSKEY-GUI 1 "October 2026" "localpasskey 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
localpasskey-gui \- window for browsing and removing the passkeys stored on this computer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B localpasskey-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B localpasskey-gui
opens a window listing the passkeys that
.BR localpasskeyd (8)
keeps for you, one per website account, in the QDarkStyle Qt theme also used
by Electrum and Feather Wallet. It is in the applications menu as
.BR LocalPasskey .
.PP
Selecting a passkey shows its website, account, whether it is a passkey
(signs you in without a username) or a security key (a second step after your
password), and when it was created and last used. From there, the Passkey menu
or a right-click, you can copy the username, open the website, or delete the
passkey. Deleting asks for confirmation, and then for your password. Remove the
passkey from your account settings on the website as well.
.PP
The list follows the service: passkeys you create in a browser appear within
a few seconds.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
Ctrl+F
Search by website or account; Escape clears the search.
.TP
Ctrl+C
Copy the username of the selected passkey.
.TP
Delete
Delete the selected passkey.
.TP
F5
Refresh the list.
.TP
Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR localpasskey (1),
.BR localpasskeyd (8)
